From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom: check for L2 only when suspending a host with wakeup

In peripheral mode the core disconnects and powers the PHY off before the
glue suspends, so the link never enters L2 and every system suspend
logged "port-1 HS-PHY not in L2" on the Galaxy Z Flip3. Check only for a
host with wakeup, the one case that parks the PHY in L2.

This is Fabricio Akio's patch of the same name (Reviewed-by and
Tested-by from Pankaj Patil, "fine as is" from Thinh Nguyen), written
again from its description because its diff could not be fetched here.

Link: https://lkml.rescloud.iu.edu/2610.2/17424.html
Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index ac68b42..2666793 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -343,10 +343,16 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_suspend(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom, bool wakeup)
 	if (qcom->is_suspended)
 		return 0;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < qcom->num_ports; i++) {
-		val = readl(qcom->qscratch_base + pwr_evnt_irq_stat_reg[i]);
-		if (!(val & PWR_EVNT_LPM_IN_L2_MASK))
-			dev_err(qcom->dev, "port-%d HS-PHY not in L2\n", i + 1);
+	/*
+	 * Only a host with wakeup parks the PHY in L2. In peripheral mode the
+	 * core disconnects and powers the PHY off before the glue suspends.
+	 */
+	if (dwc3_qcom_is_host(qcom) && wakeup) {
+		for (i = 0; i < qcom->num_ports; i++) {
+			val = readl(qcom->qscratch_base + pwr_evnt_irq_stat_reg[i]);
+			if (!(val & PWR_EVNT_LPM_IN_L2_MASK))
+				dev_err(qcom->dev, "port-%d HS-PHY not in L2\n", i + 1);
+		}
 	}
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(qcom->num_clocks, qcom->clks);
 
